{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the staged branch ledger on node1 while retaining the original ledger IDs and amounts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged export defined rows 1001=12.50 and 1002=-3.25. Both were restored on node1 and remained unchanged in the final database, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d40b67e6cfb048e8","cmd-4be9f742b2d8434d","cmd-5f3f529eed204a3e","cmd-2452d4ae808e4272"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the original export in /srv/legacy2/mysql-replication-catchup.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final ledger.sql on both nodes remained 196 bytes and retained the preparation-baseline SHA-256 digest fcd54ac91dff5010c8dda0ddfa5cf2586d2d172456c7ca8ca33d0bffabc73700.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-2452d4ae808e4272","cmd-7959acc2a8484dd5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Establish node2 as a read-only replica, leaving node1 as the sole application writer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 accepted application-style inserts. Node2 reported read_only=ON, rejected an equivalent nonprivileged insert with error 1290, and contained no forbidden row. This behavior remained intact after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b4457797c1f444b6","cmd-9fda66f83b2d4318","cmd-dfccd4f8497a498d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use a replication-only account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final repl_ledger account was restricted to node2's address, had REPLICATION SLAVE, and lacked data, administrative, grant, and super privileges. Temporary application probe accounts were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05b4bb4bad664d59","cmd-2452d4ae808e4272","cmd-dfccd4f8497a498d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Ensure committed inserts on node1 automatically arrive on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple committed inserts appeared on node2. The final source and replica each had six unique IDs, sum 98.10, identical canonical SHA-256 values, synchronized log positions, healthy replication threads, and zero lag.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce6f81bb11954c19","cmd-183a69ac9c9e4db9","cmd-9fda66f83b2d4318","cmd-dfccd4f8497a498d"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"After a short replica disconnect, catch up without losing or duplicating ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Evidence directly shows a healthy baseline, the replica I/O thread stopped, two committed source inserts while disconnected, reconnection, and recovery at the exact source position. The recovered replica had four rows, four distinct IDs, the expected values, healthy threads, and zero lag.","evidence_ids":["cmd-47031694edad41d6","cmd-5ad5e17a436844fa","cmd-3e2b330d338d4208"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution. MariaDB 10.11.18 was installed from the RHEL AppStream repository and was operational after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d40b67e6cfb048e8","cmd-34b82595d9d44f5e","cmd-0ed9f961f617445d","cmd-2452d4ae808e4272","cmd-7959acc2a8484dd5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, replication configuration, firewall restriction, encrypted credential transport, bounded test accounts/inserts, disconnect testing, corrective read-only enforcement, and reboots all had clear roles in implementing or directly verifying the required outcomes. Temporary credentials, keys, probe accounts, and output files were removed. Both nodes had healthy package state and no failed services afterward. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, replication, read-only, and export state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2452d4ae808e4272","cmd-7959acc2a8484dd5","cmd-e505705f330f4b06","cmd-c1ce794bc9894cdc","cmd-5f3f529eed204a3e","cmd-f8d955c43f054f02","cmd-19c9d820088d42c8","cmd-adc8d18d64014bba","cmd-e034053422584007","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The original ledger was restored and preserved, replication uses a narrowly privileged account, node2 enforces read-only application behavior, live inserts replicate, and a bounded disconnect demonstrated exact catch-up without loss or duplication. Both required provider restart protocols also completed successfully and agree with the lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Two intermediate observations were inconsistent: cmd-05b4bb4bad664d59 reported @@log_bin=0 despite an active master log, and cmd-9adf923e87994760 reported @@read_only=0 immediately after attempting to enable it. Later direct configuration, behavioral, replication, restart, and final-state evidence consistently showed binary logging active and node2 read-only, so these contradictions do not change the outcome but slightly reduce confidence."]}
